>> title: Jollof Rice
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, tomato, west african, one-pot
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: jollof, party rice, Nigerian jollof, Ghanaian jollof
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 15 min

>> step: blend smooth
Blend @plum tomatoes{1%lb}(450 g; cored), @red bell pepper{1%large}(seeded), and @scotch bonnet chile{1}(stemmed) to a smooth purée in a #blender{}.

>> step: fry 4 min
Fry @tomato paste{3%Tbs} and @red onion{1%small}(sliced) in @vegetable oil{1/3%cup}(80 mL) in a #Dutch oven{} for ~{4%min}.

>> step: cook down 20 min
Cook @&(~2)pepper purée{} into @&(~1)paste{} with @curry powder{1%tsp} and @dried thyme{1%tsp} until thick and darkened, ~{20%min}.

>> step: stir in
Stir @long-grain parboiled rice{2%cups}(400 g; rinsed) into @&(~1)stew base{} with @chicken stock{2%cups}(475 mL) and @kosher salt{2%tsp}.

>> step: steam covered 30 min, rest
Steam @&(~1)pot{} covered over low heat for ~{30%min}, then rest off the heat ~{10%min} and fluff with a #fork{}.
